id: yawn:protocol:orientation-framework-v1
kind: yawn.constitution
version: 1.0.0
status: working-draft
title: "YAWN Orientation Framework V1"

purpose: >
  Define the smallest public protocol needed to preserve how an attributed
  Agent receives from and acts into an Arena without collapsing observation,
  interpretation, intention, expression, consequence, proof, or authority.

constitutional_sentence: >
  An Agent observes an Arena, orients within it, selects an Intention, and
  projects an expression or attempt back into that same Arena. The resulting
  consequences become new Observations. A .yawn preserves the sources,
  distinctions, authority, and revisions across that passage.

compact_loop:
  - signal
  - orientation
  - choice
  - move
  - proof
  - update

semantic_passage:
  - observation
  - orientation
  - value_goal_or_lacuna
  - choice
  - intention
  - projection
  - consequence
  - observation_prime
  - proof_and_replay
  - update

definitions:
  agent: >
    An attributed human, collective, institution, software system, model, or
    tool represented with explicit capabilities, limits, and authority.
  agent_space: >
    The root context in which an Agent's records, membership, authority, and
    privacy are resolved.
  arena: >
    A provisional, purpose-framed slice of the world in which observations,
    intentions, projections, and consequences can be related.
  observation: >
    What became available to an attributed Agent from within an Arena, under
    particular conditions and limits. An Observation is an acquisition event;
    it is not the same object as a statement describing or interpreting it.
  orientation: >
    The Agent's revisable working model of what is happening, what matters,
    what is missing, and which possibilities remain open.
  intention: >
    The Agent's presently selected or endorsed direction: what it means to
    understand, communicate, preserve, test, repair, change, or do.
  projection: >
    What the Agent actually expresses, represents, proposes, commits, or
    attempts back into an Arena.
  move: >
    A Projection selected as an attempt to change or preserve a condition.
  consequence: >
    What the Arena and reality return, whether or not it matches the Agent's
    Intention, Projection, or prediction.
  proof: >
    An explicit method and receipt for checking a prediction, condition, or
    claimed consequence against evidence and a falsifier.
  view: >
    A rebuildable rendering of canonical records for a purpose. A View can
    change inclusion, layout, aggregation, or salience; it cannot change
    identity, epistemic status, authority, privacy, proof, or event history.

projection_kinds:
  - expression
  - claim
  - model
  - question
  - communication
  - proposal
  - commitment
  - move

invariants:
  - "The same Arena can be observed and acted into."
  - "Intention is not Projection."
  - "Projection is not Consequence."
  - "Every Move is a Projection; not every Projection is a Move."
  - "Observation acquisition is distinct from attributed statement representation."
  - "A Yawn may have no endorsed Intention, Projection, Target, or Move."
  - "An AI inference remains attributed to the inference-producing Agent or run."
  - "Targets are optional and separately ratified."
  - "A Move cannot prove itself."
  - "No proposal becomes canonical without rightful approval."
  - "Child authority is a subset of parent authority plus an explicit grant."
  - "Views never mutate canonical state or widen authority."
  - "Reality is not serialized exhaustively and may disconfirm every model."

system_roles:
  dot_yawn: "portable holonic record and open protocol"
  yawn_bot: "holonic interface and authority-bounded action agent"
  yawn_ai: "intelligence and orientation compiler that produces attributed proposals"

proof:
  requires:
    - "Observation, Intention, Projection, and Consequence remain separately addressable."
    - "Every outward action resolves to an Authority Grant or remains proposed."
    - "Every accepted update can replay to the same materialized-state hash."
    - "Every public View omits private source bodies and preserves redaction receipts."
  falsifiers:
    - "An implementation treats intended meaning as the actual projection."
    - "An implementation treats a projection as its consequence."
    - "A renderer becomes a second state store."
    - "AI testimony is attributed to the cited human rather than the inference run."

authority:
  mutation_authorized: false
  external_effects_authorized: false
  adoption_requires: "authenticated authorized decision plus append-only receipt"
